  "body": "As [Temporal](https://github.com/tc39/proposal-temporal) nears completion and is now shipping in Firefox Nightly, you could consider accepting cookie expiration times as Temporal.Instant or Temporal.ZonedDateTime objects.\n\nInstead of this:\n```js\ncookieStore.set({\n    name: 'foo',\n    value: 'bar',\n    expires: Temporal.Now.instant().add({hours: 24}).epochMilliseconds,\n});\n```\n...we could have this:\n```js\ncookieStore.set({\n    name: 'foo',\n    value: 'bar',\n    expires: Temporal.Now.instant().add({hours: 24}),\n});\n```\nThe latter seems preferable because the programmer doesn't have to remember that a DOMHighResTimeStamp is in milliseconds.",
